  - m_Id: 27915474559864854
    m_Localized: Space Cultivator
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474564059136
    m_Localized: Carries power normally. Hold it or wear engineering goggles to see
      and handle it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474564059137
    m_Localized: Copper wire with a concealing sheath. It carries power normally;
      hold it or wear engineering goggles to see and handle it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474564059138
    m_Localized: When held or worn over the eyes, reveals hidden wires and lets you
      interact with them. Can be worn with a helmet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474564059139
    m_Localized: Large debris left when a hull breaks apart. It records the original
      components and inventory; attack it to salvage and release its contents.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474564059140
    m_Localized: A packed snowball dug up with a shovel. Right-click to place it;
      each snowball adds one snow layer. Stack layers, then shovel them back up.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447744
    m_Localized: Crafted from four planks and two logs. Walk into the placed raft
      to push it. On land or in water, point at it and press F to board. Use the
      directional keys or stick to row without spending stamina; hold Shift to row
      faster at the running stamina cost. Point at the raft and press F to dismount,
      landing on nearby ground when possible or in the water otherwise.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447745
    m_Localized: A white outline appears when the cursor points at the raft. On land
      or in water, point at the raft and press F to board or dismount. Normal rowing
      uses no stamina; hold Shift while moving to spend stamina and row faster. Pointing
      at reachable seawater still lets F interact with the water and drink. The raft
      drifts with currents. Dismounting far offshore puts you in the water if no
      land is nearby. A loaded save restores it as an empty raft.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447746
    m_Localized: Place it in a crucible and heat it to the right temperature to melt
      it into molten glass.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447747
    m_Localized: Transparent glass formed by cooling and solidifying molten glass.
      Used to make glass products.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447748
    m_Localized: Holds solid materials such as sand and ore, and can also store hot
      liquids. A heat source heats only the crucible; its contents melt or transform
      according to their own temperature and reaction properties.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447749
    m_Localized: Hold the attack button to charge, then blow into the microphone.
      Releasing fires one arrow from the same inventory. Louder blows make arrows
      fly faster and add up to 100% damage.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447750
    m_Localized: A throwing tool made from rope and leather. Stones in the hotbar
      and suitable hard ores can be used as sling ammunition. Hold the attack button
      to charge and show the trajectory, then release to throw. Projectiles can be
      picked up after landing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447751
    m_Localized: Coarse fiber stripped from plant skins. A basic material for rope
      and other survival items.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474572447752
    m_Localized: A heavy slab mined from a large stone deposit or a cave entrance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642048
    m_Localized: Flammable organic soil dug from wetlands. Can be used as a low-temperature
      fuel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642049
    m_Localized: A wooden mechanical part made by drilling a through-hole in a plank.
      Used for the structure and connections of mechanical torque devices.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642050
    m_Localized: A stone mechanical part made by drilling a through-hole in a slab.
      Used for the structure and connections of mechanical torque devices.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642051
    m_Localized: A stone mechanical part made by drilling a through-hole in a stone.
      Used in mechanical torque devices.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642052
    m_Localized: Ash left after burning plant matter, used as a lightweight basic
      processing material.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642053
    m_Localized: Adds pages to readable notes.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642054
    m_Localized: A metal nail forged from wrought iron ingots. Used to fasten wood
      and mechanical structures.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642055
    m_Localized: An iron plate forged from wrought iron ingots. Used in further metalworking.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642056
    m_Localized: A plate hand-forged from pig iron ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642057
    m_Localized: A plate forged from copper ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642058
    m_Localized: A plate forged from bronze ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642059
    m_Localized: A plate forged from tin ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642060
    m_Localized: A plate forged from steel ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642061
    m_Localized: Fine coal powder made by grinding coal ore in a stone mortar. Used
      for further material processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642062
    m_Localized: Copper ore powder made by grinding malachite in a stone mortar.
      Used for further material processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642063
    m_Localized: Iron ore powder made by grinding iron ore in a stone mortar. Used
      for further material processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642064
    m_Localized: Tin ore powder made by grinding tin ore in a stone mortar. Used
      for further material processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474576642065
    m_Localized: Stone powder made by grinding stone in a stone mortar. Used for
      further material processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836352
    m_Localized: Fine niter powder made by grinding niter in a stone mortar. Used
      to make fertilizer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836353
    m_Localized: Golden natural beeswax produced by beehives. It can be eaten directly
      and is rich in carbohydrates and vitamins, but reduces water by 5.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836354
    m_Localized: A metal nail forged from steel ingots. When used with steel plates
      to craft a mechanical hammer or sawmill, it increases the finished machine's
      efficiency by 20%.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836355
    m_Localized: An egg laid by small birds and seagulls. It can be picked up, eaten,
      or cooked. Each bird can lay one at most every two days.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836356
    m_Localized: "A filament made by heating thin thread to 500\xB0C until it carbonizes.
      Combine it with glass, copper plate, and wrought iron ingot at a workbench
      to make a light bulb."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836357
    m_Localized: A piece of fabric woven from cotton. Used as a crafting material.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836358
    m_Localized: A long, flexible natural fiber that can be woven into silk.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836359
    m_Localized: A soft, lightweight fabric woven from silk fiber. Used as a crafting
      material.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836360
    m_Localized: Lightweight plastic sheet material with a smooth surface that is
      easy to shape.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836361
    m_Localized: A thin silicon sheet with a smooth, dark gray surface.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836362
    m_Localized: A refined metal bar used for crafting.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836363
    m_Localized: Gold-bearing ore that can be smelted into gold ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836364
    m_Localized: Gold ore powder made by grinding gold ore in a stone mortar. Used
      for further material processing.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836365
    m_Localized: A gold-bearing vein that must be mined with a pickaxe. Mining drops
      gold ore.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836366
    m_Localized: Rare ore mined from a diamond deposit. Can be picked up, stacked
      and stored as a material.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836367
    m_Localized: A rare diamond vein in underground caves. Drops diamond ore when
      mined. No tool tier is required; mining efficiency depends on damage, defense
      and tool harvesting bonuses.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836368
    m_Localized: Sharp black stone scattered along the shore of mountaintop lava
      lakes. Can be used as a handheld knife or crafted into an obsidian dagger or
      spear.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836369
    m_Localized: An obsidian deposit beside a mountaintop lava lake. Mine it with
      a pickaxe to obtain obsidian; there is no minimum tool tier.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836370
    m_Localized: A small blade for close combat.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836371
    m_Localized: A spear with an obsidian point. Uses the standard spear thrust attack.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836372
    m_Localized: An iron bucket that can hold water or hot magma. Place it on the
      ground to catch rain; dismantling it preserves the liquid and rain collection
      progress.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836373
    m_Localized: An open iron bucket placed on the ground. It catches rain and can
      be dismantled without losing its liquid, temperature, or rain collection progress.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836374
    m_Localized: Mineral deposits scattered around mountains and mountain lava vents.
      Can also be obtained by mining sulfur deposits.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836375
    m_Localized: Sulfur ore found in mountains and around mountain lava vents. Mining
      drops sulfur; pickaxes improve yield, with no minimum tool tier.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474580836376
    m_Localized: A wild beehive beside a forest tree, with a golden wax layer and
      a dark entrance.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224960
    m_Localized: A few wildflowers gathered from a grass flower layer with scissors.
      Can be picked up and stacked.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224961
    m_Localized: A huge natural stone deposit with the same mining behavior and drops
      as a regular stone deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224962
    m_Localized: A huge natural coal deposit with the same mining behavior and drops
      as a regular coal deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224963
    m_Localized: A huge natural copper deposit with the same mining behavior and
      drops as a regular copper deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224964
    m_Localized: A huge natural iron deposit with the same mining behavior and drops
      as a regular iron deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224965
    m_Localized: A huge natural tin deposit with the same mining behavior and drops
      as a regular tin deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224966
    m_Localized: A huge natural niter deposit with the same mining behavior and drops
      as a regular niter deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224967
    m_Localized: A huge natural diamond deposit with the same mining behavior and
      drops as a regular diamond deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224968
    m_Localized: A huge natural gold deposit with the same mining behavior and drops
      as a regular gold deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224969
    m_Localized: A huge natural obsidian deposit with the same mining behavior and
      drops as a regular obsidian deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224970
    m_Localized: A huge natural sulfur deposit with the same mining behavior and
      drops as a regular sulfur deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224971
    m_Localized: A huge natural tungsten deposit with the same mining behavior and
      drops as a regular tungsten deposit. Mine continuously from its edge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224972
    m_Localized: A dead tree that can be chopped down for logs and sticks.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224973
    m_Localized: Aim at a nearby grass layer. When a white square appears, right-click
      or tap to cut one tile of grass and collect 2 plant fibers. Scissors can also
      harvest wildflowers.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224974
    m_Localized: A wooden mechanical part made by drilling a through-hole in a stick.
      Used as a shaft core and connector in mechanical torque devices.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224975
    m_Localized: A heavy hammer with a stone head and wooden handle. More powerful
      than a wooden hammer, but each swing costs more stamina.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474589224976
    m_Localized: Hand Crank.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419264
    m_Localized: Hand Crank.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419265
    m_Localized: Water Wheel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419266
    m_Localized: Water Wheel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419267
    m_Localized: Windmill.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419268
    m_Localized: Windmill.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419269
    m_Localized: Wooden Shaft.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419270
    m_Localized: Wooden Shaft.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419271
    m_Localized: Only the short shaft on its left connects to a drive shaft. Its
      teeth mesh with adjacent gears.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419272
    m_Localized: When placed, only the short shaft on its left connects to a drive
      shaft. Its teeth mesh with adjacent gears.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419273
    m_Localized: "Gearbox building. Input through the large gear outputs 2\xD7 speed
      and 0.5\xD7 torque; input through the small gear outputs 0.5\xD7 speed and
      2\xD7 torque."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419274
    m_Localized: "When placed, input through the large gear outputs 2\xD7 speed and
      0.5\xD7 torque; input through the small gear outputs 0.5\xD7 speed and 2\xD7
      torque."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419275
    m_Localized: Clutch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474593419276
    m_Localized: Clutch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613568
    m_Localized: Shaft Bridge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613569
    m_Localized: Shaft Bridge.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613570
    m_Localized: Millstone.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613571
    m_Localized: Millstone.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613572
    m_Localized: "Point the outlet at an adjacent furnace or blast furnace to raise
      its maximum temperature based on speed. At 20 RPM it adds up to 300\xB0C; only
      the higher bonus from the bellows or oxygen-assisted combustion applies."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613573
    m_Localized: "Point the outlet at an adjacent furnace or blast furnace to raise
      its maximum temperature based on speed. At 20 RPM it adds up to 300\xB0C; only
      the higher bonus from the bellows or oxygen-assisted combustion applies."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613574
    m_Localized: Sawmill.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613575
    m_Localized: Sawmill.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613576
    m_Localized: Connect it to mechanical power to weave materials. Cotton can be
      woven into cloth and silk into silk; higher speed makes processing faster.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613577
    m_Localized: Connect it to mechanical power after placing it to weave automatically.
      The loom provides the weaving operation; the input materials determine the
      output and work required.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613578
    m_Localized: Driven by mechanical power, it forges pig iron into wrought iron
      and hammers wrought iron, copper, bronze, tin, and steel ingots into matching
      plates.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613579
    m_Localized: A mechanical hammer that connects to a drive shaft and automatically
      processes pig iron, wrought iron, copper, bronze, tin, and steel ingots.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613580
    m_Localized: A one-slot tool cabinet. Workbenches within eight adjacent cells
      can use its slot as a sixth material slot. A workbench cannot receive this
      bonus from more than one cabinet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613581
    m_Localized: A one-slot tool cabinet. Workbenches within eight adjacent cells
      can use its slot as a sixth material slot. A workbench cannot receive this
      bonus from more than one cabinet.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613582
    m_Localized: An elastic, well-insulated material used to make wires.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613583
    m_Localized: Connect a wire to the left and a drive shaft to the right. When
      powered it outputs mechanical power; when mechanically driven it outputs electricity.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613584
    m_Localized: Connect a wire to the left and a drive shaft to the right. When
      powered it outputs mechanical power; when mechanically driven it outputs electricity.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613585
    m_Localized: A copper wire for connecting electrical equipment.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613586
    m_Localized: A copper wire for connecting electrical equipment, made from copper
      and rubber.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613587
    m_Localized: Stores surplus power from the grid and discharges automatically
      when generation is insufficient.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613588
    m_Localized: Stores surplus power from the grid and discharges automatically
      when generation is insufficient.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613589
    m_Localized: Lights automatically when connected to a copper wire in the same
      cell and turns off without power. Its radius is 16 tiles, twice that of a torch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613590
    m_Localized: Lights automatically when connected to a copper wire in the same
      cell and turns off without power. Its radius is 16 tiles, twice that of a torch.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613591
    m_Localized: An oak tree that grows in forests and can yield rubber in the same
      way that resin is collected.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613592
    m_Localized: A hand-operated drilling tool that can be placed to open its drilling
      work panel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613593
    m_Localized: A portable hand drill. When placed, it shares the hand drill's work
      state.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613594
    m_Localized: Plant it to grow cotton.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613595
    m_Localized: Harvest cotton fibers when mature.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613596
    m_Localized: A juicy cactus chunk with its spines removed. Eat it to restore
      40 water and a small amount of nutrition.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474597613597
    m_Localized: A drought-tolerant plant that grows in arid deserts, not on wet
      beaches or riverbanks. Touching it causes puncture damage. Mature plants yield
      edible, hydrating cactus chunks and can also be cleared with a weapon.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002176
    m_Localized: A simple bed tied from dry grass and rope. Place it on the ground
      to sleep.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002177
    m_Localized: A grass bed that occupies two adjacent cells. Sleep in it like a
      tent.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002178
    m_Localized: A naturally formed surface cave entrance. Destroying it blocks the
      corresponding underground exit.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002179
    m_Localized: Foxtail seeds made by grinding foxtail grass in a stone mortar.
      Plant them on valid farmland; they can also be eaten directly.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002180
    m_Localized: Grind five foxtail seeds in a stone mortar to make one portion of
      flour. It can be eaten directly for carbohydrates and protein, but consumes
      water.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002181
    m_Localized: Right-click six times to dig grass, sand, or peat tiles. Can also
      dig clay deposits on riverbanks.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002182
    m_Localized: Right-click three times to dig grass, sand, or peat tiles. Can also
      dig clay deposits on riverbanks.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002183
    m_Localized: A transitional shovel made from raw iron. Digs faster than a copper
      shovel, but the metal has not been fully refined.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002184
    m_Localized: A durable bronze shovel that digs grass, sand, peat, and riverbank
      clay faster.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002185
    m_Localized: A durable wrought-iron shovel forged from iron. Suitable for extended
      digging and harvesting clay.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002186
    m_Localized: A chat command manual obtained with /help. It contains one piece
      of charcoal. Hold it and use it to read and edit the manual.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002187
    m_Localized: A wooden floor laid over ordinary land. It changes only the surface
      appearance; dismantling it restores the original tile.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474606002188
    m_Localized: A stone floor laid over ordinary land. It changes only the surface
      appearance; dismantling it restores the original tile.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196480
    m_Localized: A copper floor laid over ordinary land. It changes only the surface
      appearance; dismantling it restores the original tile.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196481
    m_Localized: An iron floor laid over ordinary land. It changes only the surface
      appearance; dismantling it restores the original tile.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196482
    m_Localized: A bronze floor laid over ordinary land. It changes only the surface
      appearance; dismantling it restores the original tile.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196483
    m_Localized: Right-click to choose a body part. After 3 seconds of setting, it
      immediately restores 10 durability, then restores another 10 after 144 seconds.
      Splints do not stack on the same body part and do not restore health.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196484
    m_Localized: Use while held to bandage the head or torso, restoring 10 points
      of part durability. Does not restore health.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196485
    m_Localized: Soft wool sheared from sheep. Use it to make cloth.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196486
    m_Localized: A water barrel sealed with planks, rope, and resin. Holds water
      and six item stacks. Add ten portions of salt to a full barrel of fresh water
      to make brine. Using resin glue to craft it increases maximum durability by
      50%.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196487
    m_Localized: A water barrel placed on the ground. Dismantle it without losing
      its liquid, stored items, or durability quality.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196488
    m_Localized: Right-click to set a hook and one piece of bait. Left-click to cast;
      after a small fish takes the bait, left-click again to reel it in.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196489
    m_Localized: Attach it to a fishing rod's hook slot and add one food item as
      bait. It can be cast 10 times. Each successful cast consumes 1 durability;
      it breaks when durability runs out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196490
    m_Localized: Attach it to a fishing rod's hook slot and add one food item as
      bait. It can be cast 100 times. Each successful cast consumes 1 durability;
      it breaks when durability runs out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196491
    m_Localized: Attach it to a fishing rod's hook slot and add one food item as
      bait. It can be cast 1,000 times. Each successful cast consumes 1 durability;
      it breaks when durability runs out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196492
    m_Localized: Moves dropped items on the ground when connected to mechanical power.
      Rotate the building to change direction; reversing power reverses transport.
      Rated for 20 RPM and 0.8 tiles per second.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196493
    m_Localized: Moves dropped items on the ground when connected to mechanical power.
      Rotate the building to change direction; reversing power reverses transport.
      Rated for 20 RPM and 0.8 tiles per second.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196494
    m_Localized: A cloth belt connects the rollers and carries items; a wooden frame
      supports it. When powered, it moves dropped items on the ground. Rotate the
      building to change direction; reversing power reverses transport. Rated for
      20 RPM and 0.8 tiles per second.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196495
    m_Localized: A cloth belt connects the rollers and carries items; a wooden frame
      supports it. When powered, it moves dropped items on the ground. Rotate the
      building to change direction; reversing power reverses transport. Rated for
      20 RPM and 0.8 tiles per second.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196496
    m_Localized: A gas and liquid pipe laid on a separate overlay layer. It can share
      a cell with wires and automatically connects to adjacent pipes and matching
      equipment ports. Silver-blue pipes and teal collars identify fluid lines; pipes
      can be stacked in the inventory.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27915474610196497
